      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Reassignment is directly relevant to resolution inefficiency, a strong analytical axis. However the short_description/timestamps do not encode reassignment history; the true/false values appear inferred without textual support and are not derivable from the shown source fields."
    },
    {
      "name": "requires_physical_intervention",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Physical intervention plausibly correlates with slower resolution, giving useful grouping. Mostly a warranted inference from asset/issue type, though it is a derived judgment rather than stated fact, introducing some uncertainty."
    },
    {
      "name": "resolution_action_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Resolution action is highly relevant to the efficiency query. But the source text describes the problem, not the resolution taken; assigning specific actions like 'repair'/'replacement' is largely inferred and asserts specifics the text does not confirm."
    },
    {
      "name": "recurrence_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.3,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Recurrence is a compelling driver of inefficiency and would be valuable. Yet nothing in the provided source text signals recurrence; the 160 true values appear invented, contradicting the silence of the text."
