      "name": "urgency_signal",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.65,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Urgency categorization is useful and partly redundant with existing priority column, but the multi-level signal from wording ('lost', 'unable') adds nuance. Inference from tone words is somewhat subjective but generally warranted."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
  "source_groundedness": 0.62,
  "rationale": "Most columns provide genuine grouping/modeling axes for diagnosing inefficient resolution (category, subtype, reassignment, action type, recurrence, urgency), with only affected_asset_type and software_trigger_present being partly redundant. The main weakness is groundedness: several high-value columns (reassignment_flag, resolution_action_type, recurrence_signal) assert specifics the problem-only source text cannot support, indicating invented rather than extracted values."
